      "object_id" : "DF92B98E-E045-4181-A5B4-B039B327B3BF",
      "text" : "- Every remote object has a name that is unique within the scope of its peers, just like plain objects\n- Remote objects do not have subobjects or methods of their own\n- Remote objects forward all requests for subobjects or method invocations over a transport\n- Transports communicate in JSON using a predefined schema",
