    {
      "alignment" : 0,
      "doc_ref" : "D9087392-A0DF-4114-82D4-AAF1AC711DDC",
      "object_id" : "F316DAB6-8434-4F93-B8F2-C160D34AF4B5",
      "text" : "- A protocol is an agreed-upon programming interface\n- Protocols have unique names shared across code spaces\n- Every protocol has a version in addition to a name, they follow semantic versioning\n- A protocol may have zero or more methods\n  - Methods have a name called a selector\n  - Selectors are unique within an object\n  - Methods accept arbitrary parameters\n  - Parameters are checked by a schema\n- An object may advertise conformance with to number of protocols",
      "type_id" : 27
    },
